      "writtenOn": "2020-11-18T15:29:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For any Unknown/unsupported ME, I would not rely upon any attributes.  The multiByteField is just a way to encode attributes that do not closely match native integer sizes.  \n\nI had first tried to define each as a multibyte that spanned 28 octets so that all the attribute data could be viewed.  This was problematic since the actual attribute decode comes after the ME definition selection.  With a larger octet span, the attribute decode fails with a truncation message if more than one bit is set in the attribute mask.  So I had to fall back to a single octet so that decode was always successful.",
      "parentUuid": "a55b0719_ac21a4a0",
      "revId": "8a5379a5c2dd84330b61699d9c4969f1f6c551e4",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
